# rbtv-ignite.service — machine-agnostic systemd USER unit template for the ignite daemon.
#
# The daemon boots from a detached deploy worktree (D6, 2026-08-19): ExecStart and
# RBTV_IGNITE_CONFIG_PATH resolve into @@DEPLOY_ROOT@@. RBTV_IGNITE_SRC still names
# the live per-invocation tree (coord/, coord.py), not the booted one.
# Per-instance values are substituted at install time.
#
# Install-time substitution points (replace each @@NAME@@ with the instance value):
#   @@WORKSPACE_ROOT@@    - workspace root: the folder that roots .rbtv/
#   @@NODE_BIN@@          - absolute path to the Node.js 24 binary
#   @@IGNITE_SRC@@        - absolute path to the LIVE ignite module source root
#                           (RBTV_IGNITE_SRC — per-invocation tree, not the booted one)
#   @@DEPLOY_ROOT@@       - absolute path to the detached deploy worktree
#                           (ExecStart + RBTV_IGNITE_CONFIG_PATH resolve here)
#   @@WORKDIR_ROOT@@      - default workdir root every spawn falls back to (REQUIRED, D22:
#                           the seed config ships only a placeholder for this, so the daemon
#                           refuses to boot until a real per-instance value is supplied)
#   @@ENVIRONMENT_FILE@@  - optional EnvironmentFile path (use /dev/null to disable)
#
# Per-instance values reach the daemon through this unit and/or the EnvironmentFile —
# NEVER by editing config/spawn-profiles.yaml in the repo, which would write an instance
# path into the code tree (D26(3)).  EnvironmentFile= settings override Environment=
# (systemd.exec), so the file is the operator's override surface; RBTV_IGNITE_DATA_ROOT
# and RBTV_IGNITE_CARRIER are set there when the seed defaults do not fit.
#
# StateDirectory= provisions %S/rbtv-ignite (the runtime data root) for the user unit.
# In a user unit %S resolves to $XDG_STATE_HOME (~/.local/state).  The unit exports this
# path as RBTV_IGNITE_DATA_ROOT so the seed config's system-centric /var/lib/rbtv-ignite
# is overridden without editing the committed config.  An operator who moves data_root off
# the default via the EnvironmentFile owns creating that path.
#
# Install location for the user manager:
#   ~/.config/systemd/user/rbtv-ignite.service
#
# After installing and substituting:
#   systemctl --user daemon-reload
#   systemctl --user enable rbtv-ignite
#   systemctl --user start rbtv-ignite
#
# Deploy prerequisite — PATH: the [Service] block below ships a PATH= Environment
# line covering the user-local bin dirs (~/.local/bin, ~/.opencode/bin) the agent
# harnesses install into, via the %h specifier — no substitution needed. Without it
# the daemon inherits the minimal user-manager PATH and every real agent spawn fails
# ENOENT. Verify the installed unit still carries this line before enabling.
#
# ── The boot cockpit (task 7.36, settle ledger R6/R15) ────────────────────────────────
# At boot the daemon spawns a tmux session named `rbtv-cockpit`: teamview plus a LAZY
# master pane (cd'd to place, harness NOT launched — the owner attaches and types).
# It is a tmux session, NOT a second systemd unit (the chat bridge — rbtv-chat-bridge.service
# beside this file — is the one other systemd citizen of this module). It is IDEMPOTENT (an existing cockpit is left untouched, so Restart=on-failure
# never destroys what the owner had open) and FAIL-SOFT (no tmux, no teamview, or a
# refusing tmux server logs a reason and the daemon boots normally).
# Optional EnvironmentFile knobs, none required:
#   RBTV_IGNITE_COCKPIT=off             - disable the cockpit entirely
#   RBTV_IGNITE_COCKPIT_MASTER_DIR      - master pane cwd (default: the workspace root,
#                                         where a cold session IS the console master)
#   RBTV_IGNITE_COCKPIT_PACKAGE         - pin teamview's run folder (default: the most
#                                         recently active run under .rbtv/goals/*/runs/)
#   RBTV_IGNITE_COCKPIT_TEAMVIEW        - teamview binary (default: PATH, then the
#                                         orchestration module beside ignite/)
# Deploy prerequisite: `tmux` on the PATH below. Its absence costs the cockpit only.
#
# One more optional EnvironmentFile knob, and it is a PATH — never a secret (task C3):
#   RBTV_IGNITE_CHAT_ENV_FILE           - the chat bridge's own EnvironmentFile (the one
#                                         rbtv-chat-bridge.service names), carrying
#                                         SLACK_BOT_TOKEN. Set it and the daemon causes an
#                                         INTERACTIVE goal's Slack channel to exist at that
#                                         goal's workflow start, by launching the bridge's
#                                         `goal-channel-cli.js ensure <goal>` with this file
#                                         as the CHILD's EnvironmentFile. ⚑ The daemon never
#                                         reads it: systemd does, into the child only, which
#                                         is how `goal-channel-design.md`'s bound ("the daemon
#                                         holds no chat credential and must not grow one")
#                                         survives the daemon gaining this caller. UNSET is a
#                                         supported state — the ensure is recorded as skipped
#                                         in the tick log, never attempted.
#                                         ⚑ REQUIRES THE SYSTEMD CARRIER. `EnvironmentFile=` is a
#                                         systemd property; the setsid carrier cannot set one, so
#                                         a setsid child would run the ensure with NO token. On a
#                                         non-systemd carrier the ensure is therefore SKIPPED,
#                                         reason `carrier-cannot-carry-credential`, rather than
#                                         launched — a doomed exec reported as a success is worse
#                                         than a recorded skip. This costs nothing real: every
#                                         deployment that has a bridge runs systemd already
#                                         (rbtv-chat-bridge.service is itself a unit).
#
# Do NOT commit a substituted version of this file.

# network-online.target does NOT exist for the user manager (it ships under
# /usr/lib/systemd/system, which the user manager never searches), so the After=/Wants=
# pair this unit carried as a SYSTEM unit resolved to `not-found` here and ordered nothing.
# It is dropped rather than left as a dependency that reads like a guarantee and is not one.
# The v1 bind is loopback (config bind.host 127.0.0.1), which needs no network wait. When
# p5-2 moves the bind to the tailnet, network readiness needs a REAL mechanism (bind retry
# in the daemon, or a user-manager-visible readiness unit) — not this line.
[Unit]
Description=RBTV ignite daemon

[Service]
Type=simple
WorkingDirectory=@@WORKSPACE_ROOT@@
EnvironmentFile=-@@ENVIRONMENT_FILE@@
# PATH must include the user-local bin dirs where the agent harnesses install
# (opencode → ~/.opencode/bin; claude/codex/kimi → ~/.local/bin). Without this the
# daemon inherits the minimal user-manager PATH and every real agent spawn fails
# ENOENT — only system binaries (node/python3) resolve. Added 2026-07-17 (D12 deploy).
# %h expands to the invoking user's home for a systemd USER unit — machine-agnostic,
# no @@PLACEHOLDER@@ needed.
Environment="PATH=%h/.local/bin:%h/.opencode/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/games:/usr/local/games:/snap/bin"
# RBTV_IGNITE_SRC names the live per-invocation tree (coord/, coord.py), not the booted one.
Environment="RBTV_IGNITE_SRC=@@IGNITE_SRC@@"
Environment="RBTV_IGNITE_WORKSPACE_ROOT=@@WORKSPACE_ROOT@@"
Environment="RBTV_IGNITE_CONFIG_PATH=@@DEPLOY_ROOT@@/ignite/envelope/spawn-profiles.yaml"
Environment="RBTV_IGNITE_WORKDIR_ROOT=@@WORKDIR_ROOT@@"
Environment="RBTV_IGNITE_DATA_ROOT=%S/rbtv-ignite"
Environment="RBTV_IGNITE_USER_MANAGER=true"
# Retention window (days) for the per-machine state root's ENUMERATED artifact classes
# (logs/, prompts/, exits/, ticker.log, feed.jsonl — never heart.db; `ptys/` and `ttyd.log`
# left the enumeration at task 7.29 with the pty module and the ttyd surface),
# swept at daemon boot and daily (task 7.13). 0 = never delete; values below 7 are
# REJECTED at boot (a typo must not be able to erase the audit trail). Override via the
# EnvironmentFile like any RBTV_IGNITE_* knob.
Environment="RBTV_IGNITE_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=90"
StateDirectory=rbtv-ignite
# 0700: the state root holds heart.db + logs; keep it unreadable to other local users (task 7.26).
StateDirectoryMode=0700
ExecStart=@@NODE_BIN@@ @@DEPLOY_ROOT@@/ignite/runtime/index.js
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
